I think this test is wrong. We have to test the case where the value is single.

In my opinion, we should not strip `[]` because it prevents the introduction of breaking changes. So the ideal test is as follows:

```ts
it('should parse single value as array if the key has []', async () => {
  const data = new FormData()
  data.append('foo[]', 'bar')
  const req = createRequest(FORM_URL, 'POST', data)
  expect(await parseBody(req, { all: true })).toEqual({
    'foo[]': ['bar'],
  })
})
```

